WEBVTT

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:01.843
Welcome to one two one.

00:00:01.843 --> 00:00:10.562
In this video you will learn how to use a Temp room: a private chat for exactly two people, that deletes itself when you are done.

00:00:10.562 --> 00:00:14.050
There is no account to make, and nothing to install.

00:00:15.050 --> 00:00:16.854
First, three simple ideas.

00:00:16.854 --> 00:00:20.183
The Secret Room Key is the address of your room.

00:00:20.183 --> 00:00:26.981
A Pass Code is a personal seat: each of the two people gets their own, so nobody else can come in.

00:00:26.981 --> 00:00:32.600
And the secret phrase is an optional extra lock, which we will cover in a moment.

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:36.841
A Temp room is made for a quick, private talk.

00:00:36.841 --> 00:00:38.602
It has exactly two seats.

00:00:38.602 --> 00:00:42.335
Everything you write is encrypted on your own device.

00:00:42.335 --> 00:00:46.139
When you have both left, a thirty minute timer starts.

00:00:46.139 --> 00:00:52.550
If neither of you comes back in that time, the room and every message are deleted for good.

00:00:53.550 --> 00:00:54.578
Let us begin.

00:00:54.578 --> 00:00:56.870
Open the one two one website.

00:00:56.870 --> 00:01:03.825
We recommend a Private or Incognito window, because it leaves no history on your device.

00:01:03.825 --> 00:01:08.331
You will see three tabs: Join a room, Create, and Random.

00:01:08.331 --> 00:01:09.200
Tap Create.

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:12.451
Now choose how long the room lives.

00:01:12.451 --> 00:01:13.222
Select Temp.

00:01:13.222 --> 00:01:18.560
Underneath, you can read what that means: gone thirty minutes after you both leave.

00:01:19.560 --> 00:01:21.840
When you are ready, tap Create my room.

00:01:22.840 --> 00:01:24.265
Your room is ready.

00:01:24.265 --> 00:01:31.465
You now see three things: the Secret Room Key, your own Pass Code, and your partner’s Pass Code.

00:01:31.465 --> 00:01:34.165
Important: they are shown only once.

00:01:34.165 --> 00:01:39.340
We store them only as scrambled hashes, so we cannot show them again.

00:01:39.340 --> 00:01:40.390
Copy them now.

00:01:41.390 --> 00:01:43.576
Tap Copy invite for your partner.

00:01:43.576 --> 00:01:47.817
It copies a ready message with the room key and their Pass Code.

00:01:47.817 --> 00:01:50.070
Send it through any messaging app.

00:01:50.070 --> 00:01:52.720
Never send your own Pass Code to anyone.

00:01:53.720 --> 00:01:56.460
Then tap Enter my room, to go in yourself.

00:01:57.460 --> 00:02:00.297
Next comes the optional secret phrase.

00:02:00.297 --> 00:02:03.508
You are the first person in, so you decide.

00:02:03.508 --> 00:02:08.510
Type a phrase of five to forty characters, and spaces count as one.

00:02:08.510 --> 00:02:13.961
If you set one, your partner must type exactly the same phrase to get in.

00:02:13.961 --> 00:02:18.590
It never leaves your device, so nobody can recover it for you.

00:02:19.590 --> 00:02:22.940
Or leave it empty, and tap Enter without a phrase.

00:02:22.940 --> 00:02:25.218
Then your partner simply walks in.

00:02:25.218 --> 00:02:31.986
Your messages are still encrypted, but without a phrase, our server could in theory work out the key.

00:02:31.986 --> 00:02:35.470
For anything sensitive, we recommend using a phrase.

00:02:36.470 --> 00:02:40.230
Here we typed a phrase, and tapped the eye to check it.

00:02:40.230 --> 00:02:42.418
Now tap Create phrase and enter.

00:02:42.418 --> 00:02:51.100
Share the phrase with your partner separately, ideally face to face or by phone, and never in the same message as the room key.

00:02:52.100 --> 00:02:54.429
You are inside your private room.

00:02:54.429 --> 00:02:57.392
Your partner shows as: has not joined yet.

00:02:57.392 --> 00:02:59.580
The room simply waits for them.

00:03:00.580 --> 00:03:02.149
Now the partner’s side.

00:03:02.149 --> 00:03:07.881
They open the website, and on Join a room, type the Secret Room Key from the invite.

00:03:07.881 --> 00:03:09.450
Then they tap Continue.

00:03:10.450 --> 00:03:15.381
On the next step they enter their own Pass Code, the one meant for them.

00:03:15.381 --> 00:03:19.011
It is hidden by default, and the eye button shows it.

00:03:19.011 --> 00:03:19.970
Then Continue.

00:03:20.970 --> 00:03:25.421
If a phrase was set, they now see a box, and must type it exactly.

00:03:25.421 --> 00:03:28.590
If they were not told it, they need to ask you.

00:03:29.590 --> 00:03:32.523
A wrong phrase is refused with this message.

00:03:32.523 --> 00:03:35.390
Nothing is lost, they can simply try again.

00:03:36.390 --> 00:03:39.955
If no phrase was set, they see this screen instead.

00:03:39.955 --> 00:03:41.842
There is no box to fill in.

00:03:41.842 --> 00:03:43.590
They just tap Enter room.

00:03:44.590 --> 00:03:47.635
Now you are both inside, and you can chat.

00:03:47.635 --> 00:03:52.493
You will see when your partner is online, and when they are typing.

00:03:52.493 --> 00:03:59.960
Under your messages are ticks: one tick means sent, two ticks mean delivered, and blue ticks mean seen.

00:04:00.960 --> 00:04:06.386
Press and hold a message, or use the three dots on a computer, to open its menu.

00:04:06.386 --> 00:04:10.930
React with an emoji, reply to that exact message, or copy the text.

00:04:10.930 --> 00:04:17.170
On a phone you can also swipe a message to the right to reply, just like in other chat apps.

00:04:18.170 --> 00:04:24.677
For something extra private, tap the dotted circle button beside the message box before you send.

00:04:24.677 --> 00:04:30.110
That message is view once: your partner opens it one time, and then it is erased.

00:04:31.110 --> 00:04:34.029
Vanish mode is the ghost button at the top.

00:04:34.029 --> 00:04:37.763
It is off by default, and appears once you are both in.

00:04:37.763 --> 00:04:44.077
Switch it on, and every new message disappears thirty seconds after your partner has seen it.

00:04:44.077 --> 00:04:46.250
Both of you watch the countdown.

00:04:47.250 --> 00:04:49.259
What happens when you leave?

00:04:49.259 --> 00:04:53.134
When you have both left, a thirty minute clock starts.

00:04:53.134 --> 00:04:55.933
If either of you comes back, it resets.

00:04:55.933 --> 00:05:01.386
If nobody does, the room, both seats and every message are removed for good.

00:05:01.386 --> 00:05:03.180
Nothing can restore them.

00:05:04.180 --> 00:05:05.816
A few do’s and don’ts.

00:05:05.816 --> 00:05:07.601
Do use a Private window.

00:05:07.601 --> 00:05:11.616
Do send the invite and the phrase by different routes.

00:05:11.616 --> 00:05:14.516
Do use a phrase for anything sensitive.

00:05:14.516 --> 00:05:17.044
And do leave using Leave the room.

00:05:17.044 --> 00:05:22.918
Do not share your own Pass Code, and never put the phrase next to the room key.

00:05:22.918 --> 00:05:26.116
Lost codes and phrases cannot be recovered.

00:05:26.116 --> 00:05:30.280
And please, do not use one two one for anything harmful.

00:05:31.280 --> 00:05:32.877
That is the Temp room.

00:05:32.877 --> 00:05:37.522
Create one any time at one two one dot the secret basket dot in.

00:05:37.522 --> 00:05:45.071
Watch the Long-term room video to keep a room for thirty days, and the Random video to meet someone new.

00:05:45.071 --> 00:05:46.740
Thank you for watching.
